1.Image pull back off--------
“If a pod is stuck in ImagePullBackOff state, I first troubleshoot by running kubectl describe pod <pod-name> 
and checking the Events section to identify the exact error. 
If the error shows ‘unauthorized,’ it usually means Kubernetes 
cannot authenticate with the private registry due to invalid or missing credentials. In that case, I update or recreate the imagePullSecret
with correct credentials, or verify IAM roles/permissions for the nodes.
After fixing the authentication issue, I restart the pod and confirm that the image pulls successfully.”

