10.The DatabaseTimeout (NetworkPolicy)
**“DB timeout → check NetworkPolicy → allow egress + verify cloud security group.”**
_________________
**“If the application is running but cannot connect to an external database and shows a connection timeout,
I first suspect a network restriction. I check whether a NetworkPolicy was recently applied to the namespace, 
because once a policy exists, Kubernetes blocks all traffic that isn’t explicitly allowed.**

**To fix it, I verify the NetworkPolicy has the correct egress rule allowing traffic to the database IP range and port. 
I also check the cloud security group and ensure the Kubernetes node or pod CIDR is allowed in the database’s inbound rules.**

**After updating network rules, I retest connectivity and confirm the application can reach the database.”**








